      "message": "feat(sim): draw a turning tool's lathe body at the tool position\n\nA tool carrying a lathe-frame body (#369) is now drawn in the\nsimulation and viewport as that body's own tool-frame facets, posed at\nthe playhead in the frame the holder law judges it in: the tip at the\nmove's point, +x along the op path's signed radial, +z along the\nspindle (the law's own Frame::about fit and SignedMeridian radial,\nexposed as operation::lathe_body_axes). Drawn as modelled, not\nrevolved, through the existing SimToolCache::posed seam; the fitted\nframe is cached per op, path signature and body. A lathe steel without\na body keeps the axis marker only, as before. Display only: no verdict\nchanges.\n\nFixes #1038\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
